# ==============================================================================
# Open Data Contract Standard (ODCS) v3.1.0
# Iris Customer - Silver Layer Data Contract  (DRAFT, PBI 3586168)
# Source: Fabric Lakehouse lh_bronze.mpi_bronze (Iris loads) -> Target: lh_silver dbo
#
# ASSUMPTIONS TO CONFIRM BEFORE MERGE (search for "TODO"):
#   - Silver table names and column names match the bronze names below
#   - Which Iris bronze tables feed the silver Iris load
#   - Bronze columns checked against Fabric INFORMATION_SCHEMA screenshots (10/20/2026):
#     iris_customer (20 cols), iris_events_customer_normalized (43; the _delta variant has 37),
#     iris_mapping (6), iris_rtmi_mapping (5). Every bronze column is nullable, hence the NULL guards.
#   - iris_raw_events (12 cols, JSON payloads) is not covered yet
#   - Iris id types differ across tables: string in iris_customer / iris_events_customer_normalized /
#     iris_rtmi_mapping, bigint in iris_mapping / iris_raw_events. FK checks cast; fix upstream if possible.
# Scope: hard rules only (completeness, uniqueness, ranges, formats, FK).
#        Identity-resolution business rules are out of scope (tracked with Sue Heupel / MPI).
# ==============================================================================

apiVersion: v3.1.0
kind: DataContract

id: dc-iris-customer
name: "Iris Customer - Silver Layer Data Contract"
version: 1.0.0
status: draft
domain: insurance
dataProduct: iris-customer
tenant: TruStage

# TODO: add authoritativeDefinitions url once the file path in the repo is final

description:
  purpose: Provide cleansed Iris customer records, customer events and Iris/RTMI id mappings for the Silver layer.
  limitations: Only includes Iris file loads. RTMI data is covered by a separate contract. Identity resolution is not performed here.
  usage: Used as a source for the Party Domain and the consumer key ring in the Silver layer.

schema:
